msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucid-h7-wing.rst:134
#: 9d173a1f1e694fc9be6520d65db26343
msgid "The TBS Lucid H7 Wing does not come with ArduPilot firmware pre-installed. Use the instructions here to load ArduPilot the first time :ref:`common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards`. Firmware for the TBS Lucid H7 Wing can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`_ in sub-folders labeled “TBS_LUCID_H7_WING\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucid-h7-wing.rst:137
#: 1ec399075cfe4dd28fd0ff0ec7a0b731
msgid "Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"with_bl.hex\" firmware, using your favourite DFU loading tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucid-h7-wing.rst:141
#: af90bf87218449438401d1ac7e9fe930
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \\*.apj firmware files."
msgstr ""
